topPRs.body:
Phase 6 completes the ID type system refactor by removing all backward compatibility code. This is a **breaking change** that removes ~1,200 net lines of code (2,578 deletions, 1,385 additions), leaving only the unified `ComponentID` type system.

## What This Phase Removes

### 1. Type Aliases for Backward Compatibility

From `stack/component_id.go`, removed 19 type aliases:
```go
// REMOVED - these aliases allowed old code to compile during migration
type (
    L1ELNodeID     = ComponentID
    L1CLNodeID     = ComponentID
    L2BatcherID    = ComponentID
    L2ELNodeID     = ComponentID
    // ... 15 more
)
```

### 2. `Kind` Type Alias

From `stack/component_id.go`:
```go
// REMOVED
type Kind = ComponentKind
```

### 3. Old Base Types from `stack/id.go`

Removed the original ID infrastructure (~150 lines):
```go
// REMOVED - old Kind type and methods
type Kind string
func (k Kind) LogValue() slog.Value { ... }
func (k Kind) String() string { ... }
func (k Kind) MarshalText() ([]byte, error) { ... }
func (k *Kind) UnmarshalText(data []byte) error { ... }

// REMOVED - base struct types
type idWithChain struct { key string; chainID eth.ChainID }
type idOnlyChainID struct { chainID eth.ChainID }
type genericID struct { key string }

// REMOVED - interfaces
type IDWithChain interface { ... }
type IDOnlyChainID interface { ... }
type GenericID interface { ... }

// REMOVED - helper functions
func lessIDWithChain[T IDWithChain](a, b T) bool { ... }
func lessIDOnlyChainID[T IDOnlyChainID](a, b T) bool { ... }
func lessElemOrdered[E any, ID cmp.Ordered](...) bool { ... }
func copyAndSortCmp[V ~[]E, E any](vs V, cmp func(a, b E) int) V { ... }
```

### 4. Old ID Type Definitions from Component Files

Removed ID type definitions from 19 component files. Example from `stack/l2_batcher.go`:
```go
// REMOVED (~50 lines per file)
const L2BatcherKind Kind = "L2Batcher"

type L2BatcherID idWithChain

func NewL2BatcherID(key string, chainID eth.ChainID) L2BatcherID { ... }
func (id L2BatcherID) Kind() Kind { return L2BatcherKind }
func (id L2BatcherID) Key() string { return id.key }
func (id L2BatcherID) ChainID() eth.ChainID { return id.chainID }
func (id L2BatcherID) String() string { ... }
func (id L2BatcherID) LogValue() slog.Value { ... }
func (id L2BatcherID) MarshalText() ([]byte, error) { ... }
func (id *L2BatcherID) UnmarshalText(data []byte) error { ... }
func SortL2BatcherIDs(ids []L2BatcherID) []L2BatcherID { ... }
```

Files affected: `l1_el.go`, `l1_cl.go`, `l1_network.go`, `l2_el.go`, `l2_cl.go`, `l2_network.go`, `l2_batcher.go`, `l2_proposer.go`, `l2_challenger.go`, `rollup_boost.go`, `op_rbuilder.go`, `faucet.go`, `sync_tester.go`, `supervisor.go`, `conductor.go`, `cluster.go`, `superchain.go`, `test_sequencer.go`, `fb_ws_client.go`

### 5. Old Matcher Type Aliases

From `stack/matcher.go`, removed two-parameter matcher aliases:
```go
// REMOVED
type L2BatcherMatcher = Matcher[L2BatcherID, L2Batcher]
type L2ELMatcher = Matcher[L2ELNodeID, L2ELNode]
// ... etc
```

### 6. Sort Functions

Removed 19 sort functions from component files:
```go
// REMOVED
func SortL2BatcherIDs(ids []L2BatcherID) []L2BatcherID { ... }
func SortL1NetworkIDs(ids []L1NetworkID) []L1NetworkID { ... }
// ... etc
```

Now use `ComponentID.Less()` method with standard sorting.

## What This Phase Updates

### 1. Interface Return Types

Updated `KindProvider` interface to use `ComponentKind`:
```go
// stack/id.go
type KindProvider interface {
    Kind() ComponentKind  // was: Kind() Kind
}
```

### 2. Context Functions

Updated `stack/context.go`:
```go
func ContextWithKind(ctx context.Context, kind ComponentKind) context.Context
func KindFromContext(ctx context.Context) ComponentKind
func KindSelector(kind ComponentKind) logfilter.Selector
```

### 3. Matcher Interface

Simplified from two type parameters to one:
```go
// Before
type Matcher[ID, E any] interface {
    Match(elems []E) ([]E, ID)
}

// After
type Matcher[E] interface {
    Match(elems []E) []E
}

// New helper for ID-based matching
func ByID[E Identifiable](id ComponentID) Matcher[E]
```

### 4. Shim and Sysgo Updates

All files updated to use `ComponentID` directly with typed constructors:
```go
// Example usage
id := stack.NewL2BatcherID("mynode", chainID)  // Returns ComponentID
batcher := network.L2Batcher(stack.ByID[stack.L2Batcher](id))
```

### 5. Test Files

- `stack/capabilities_test.go` - Updated constructor calls
- `stack/component_id_test.go` - Use typed constructors directly
- `stack/context_test.go` - Changed `Kind("")` to `ComponentKind("")`
- `stack/registry_test.go` - Updated type patterns

## Type System After Phase 6

### Single ID Type
```go
// Unified ID type - no wrappers or aliases
type ComponentID struct {
    kind    ComponentKind
    shape   IDShape
    key     string
    chainID eth.ChainID
}

// Typed constructor functions (return ComponentID directly)
func NewL2BatcherID(key string, chainID eth.ChainID) ComponentID
func NewL2ELNodeID(key string, chainID eth.ChainID) ComponentID
func NewL1NetworkID(chainID eth.ChainID) ComponentID
func NewSupervisorID(key string) ComponentID
// ... etc
```

### Simplified Matcher
```go
type Matcher[E] interface {
    Match(elems []E) []E
}

// Non-generic Identifiable
type Identifiable interface {
    ID() ComponentID
}

// Create matcher from ID
func ByID[E Identifiable](id ComponentID) Matcher[E]
```

### Clean Interfaces
```go
type L2Network interface {
    ID() ComponentID
    L2Batcher(m Matcher[L2Batcher]) L2Batcher
    L2BatcherIDs() []ComponentID
    // ...
}
```

